@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+---
+id: dl-006-rentals-shorter-than-a-day-on-the-hour-are-priced-per-hour
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rentals shorter than a day on the hour are priced per hour"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Context
+
+Visitors often want a board for an afternoon, and the desk turns them away because a period is only
+whole UTC days. The request adds an optional `hourlyPrice` to `addEquipment`: the price of one hour in
+euro cents. A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at that hourly price
+for each hour. An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+dl-002 fixes that a period boundary is a UTC midnight and that the price is days times `dailyPrice`.
+dl-003 says two bookings overlap when their periods share at least one day. Both now need amending for
+hourly periods. The request does not say what a period that is not whole days but is a day or longer
+should do, nor how a 10% discount would apply to hours.
+
+# Decision
+
+- `addEquipment` takes an optional `hourlyPrice`. When given, it is validated as `dailyPrice` is: a
+  non-negative safe integer of euro cents. It is not required, so an item without one can still be rented
+  by the day, and by the hour it throws.
+- A period boundary is a UTC time on the hour, written `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:00:00Z`, with an optional `.000`
+  before the `Z`. Minutes and seconds other than zero are rejected.
+- A period whose start and end are both UTC midnights is a whole-day rental, priced as before with
+  `dailyPrice`, and it gets the 10% discount from dl-005 at three days or more.
+- Any other period must be shorter than a day. A period that is not whole days and lasts a day or more
+  (for example 09:00 to 09:00 the next day) is rejected.
+- A period shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is an hourly rental. Its total is the
+  number of hours times `hourlyPrice`. It is never discounted, since it is under three days.
+- An hourly rental of an item without `hourlyPrice` throws, from `quote` and `book` alike.
+- Overlap for `book` and `availability` is the same half-open test on the instants of the periods, so it
+  works for hourly periods and day periods alike. A booking that ends at 12:00 does not block a period
+  that starts at 12:00. This amends dl-003: two periods overlap when they share any time, not only a day.
+- `quote` and `book` both get the total from the same pricing function. `book` prices the period before it
+  checks overlap or records anything, so a rejected booking does not use up a booking id.
+
+# Consequences
+
+- A visitor can rent for a few hours with one call. The hourly total is exact, with no rounding.
+- A client that sends local times must still convert them to UTC, and must send whole hours for a rental
+  that is not whole days. A period that is not on the hour, or runs a day or longer and is not whole days,
+  is refused.
+- Hourly rentals are not discounted, so a short rental costs the same per hour however often it is booked.
+- dl-002's rule that a boundary must be UTC midnight is amended: a boundary may now be any UTC hour. Its
+  rule that the price is days times `dailyPrice` still holds for whole-day periods.
+- Items without an hourly price keep their current behaviour; only hourly rentals of them are refused.
