@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+id: task-004-rent-equipment-by-the-hour
+type: task
+title: "Rent equipment by the hour"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Many visitors want a board only for an afternoon, and the desk turns them away today. Customers should be
+able to rent by the hour. `addEquipment` accepts an `hourlyPrice`, the cost of one hour in euro cents. A
+rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's hourly price for each
+hour. An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+# Work
+
+- Tests first, in `src/rental.test.ts`: hourly quote and book totals, a rental crossing midnight, an
+  hourly rental of an item without an hourly price (refused, and no booking id used up), a period not
+  whole days that lasts a day or more (refused), hourly overlap and boundaries with day bookings,
+  `availability` over hourly bookings, and validation of `hourlyPrice`. The off-the-hour and midnight
+  format tests were updated to the new rule, since `10:00` is now a valid hour.
+- Implementation in `src/rental.ts`: `hourlyPrice` on `Equipment`, validated when added; periods accept
+  UTC hours; `priceOf` prices a whole-day period as before and an hourly period per hour; `book` prices
+  before it records anything.
+- `src/rental.ts` interface doc comments, `README.md`, and dl-006 describe hourly rental.
+- The rules are recorded in dl-006, which amends dl-002 (boundaries) and dl-003 (overlap).
+
+# Result
+
+- `npm test` builds with strict TypeScript and runs 43 tests, all passing: the 32 from task-003, with
+  the three tests that used `10:00` as a non-midnight example moved to `10:30`, and 11 new ones.
+- The new tests were run first and failed to compile, since `hourlyPrice` did not exist yet.
+- Not changed: `addEquipment` for daily items, the 10% discount, and the booking id counter, which now
+  takes no id for a refused period (a refused hourly booking used to be a case the code could not reach).
+- Not decided: a cancellation, which is still not implemented, and whether an hourly rental of an item
+  with no hourly price should say why it is refused in a separate error code.
